# Design system

`docs/design-system.md` is the visual and interaction lock for the `mobile` and `web`
surfaces. `admin` and `api` are outside the lock.

When the implement append includes a **Slice design lock (excerpt)**, that excerpt is
the lock for this job. Do not read the full file unless a named AC pattern is missing
from the excerpt. When no excerpt is present, read only the Components inventory and
the specific `###` sections named in the issue — not the entire file.

Apply the lock; do not invent taste:

- Take tokens, spacing, type, motion, and component variants from the lock. If a value
  you need is missing, flag the gap on the issue instead of inventing one.
- Before adding a screen or component not named in `docs/design-system.md` Scope §Included
  or Components inventory, flag the gap on the Linear issue. Do not invent layout, tokens,
  or new primitive names (e.g. `Screen`, `FieldLabel`) — use locked tokens inline or wait
  for sign-off.
- Tab bar screens (`apps/mobile/app/(tabs)/`) use the locked floating icon-only glass pill
  (docs/design-system.md Tab bar, Gap 2026-08-23). Five slots: Samling · Søg · Tilføj trøje ·
  Ønske · Profil — icon-only chrome with Danish accessible names, no visible tab labels.
  CI enforces anatomy via `pnpm check:mobile-tab-bar`. A labeled dock or `tabBarLabel`-only bar
  is a miss.
- Type size comes from locked `type.*` roles. A raw `fontSize` in px (e.g. `fontSize: 10`)
  is an invented value — use the role or flag the gap. Same for color: no raw hex/rgba
  outside `theme/tokens.ts`.
- Mobile components must not use raw hex or `rgb`/`rgba` literals outside
  `apps/mobile/src/theme/tokens.ts`. Import semantic roles from `theme/tokens.ts` instead.
  CI enforces this via `pnpm check:mobile-design-tokens`.
- Grayscale carries hierarchy. The identity wash is garnish, never a primary CTA, chrome,
  or a status encoding.
- Marks come from data — a licensed mark or a `CatalogLabel` monogram. Never emoji, never
  an invented crest, never `KitPhoto` bytes as a club mark.
- Danish-first copy, with labels from `CatalogLabel` rather than the English seed string.
- Hit targets at least 44x44 on mobile, WCAG AA for text and essential controls, and a
  still equivalent under `prefers-reduced-motion`.

The lock outranks the code: if an existing screen contradicts `docs/design-system.md`, say
which one is the bug rather than copying the screen.
